{
  "total": 543.303,
  "scenes": [
    {
      "id": "S01",
      "start": 0.15,
      "speech_end": 3.841,
      "end": 4.641,
      "dur": 4.491,
      "text": "The last B-52 left the factory in 1962."
    },
    {
      "id": "S02",
      "start": 4.641,
      "speech_end": 10.68,
      "end": 11.28,
      "dur": 6.639,
      "text": "In some American families, three generations have flown in it. From grandfather to grandson."
    },
    {
      "id": "S03",
      "start": 11.28,
      "speech_end": 15.312,
      "end": 16.112,
      "dur": 4.832,
      "text": "And the US Air Force plans to keep flying it into the 2050s."
    },
    {
      "id": "S04",
      "start": 16.112,
      "speech_end": 19.248,
      "end": 20.048,
      "dur": 3.936,
      "text": "That's close to a hundred years after its first flight."
    },
    {
      "id": "S05",
      "start": 20.048,
      "speech_end": 26.917,
      "end": 27.417,
      "dur": 7.369,
      "text": "Along the way, it has outlived the bomber that was meant to replace it, a giant that flew at three times the speed of sound."
    },
    {
      "id": "S06",
      "start": 27.417,
      "speech_end": 30.724,
      "end": 31.924,
      "dur": 4.507,
      "text": "And it's expected to outlive the B-2 stealth bomber, too."
    },
    {
      "id": "S07",
      "start": 31.924,
      "speech_end": 36.684,
      "end": 38.284,
      "dur": 6.36,
      "text": "So why does the most powerful air force in the world keep flying its oldest bomber?"
    },
    {
      "id": "S08",
      "start": 38.284,
      "speech_end": 40.46,
      "end": 41.26,
      "dur": 2.976,
      "text": "Here's the first part of the answer."
    },
    {
      "id": "S09",
      "start": 41.26,
      "speech_end": 45.335,
      "end": 46.135,
      "dur": 4.875,
      "text": "Every one of its would-be replacements was built to be the best at something."
    },
    {
      "id": "S10",
      "start": 46.135,
      "speech_end": 49.165,
      "end": 49.965,
      "dur": 3.831,
      "text": "Faster. Higher. Harder to see on radar."
    },
    {
      "id": "S11",
      "start": 49.965,
      "speech_end": 53.805,
      "end": 54.405,
      "dur": 4.44,
      "text": "The B-52 was built to carry a lot of weight a very long way."
    },
    {
      "id": "S12",
      "start": 54.405,
      "speech_end": 57.755,
      "end": 58.555,
      "dur": 4.149,
      "text": "And being the best at something turns out to have an expiry date."
    },
    {
      "id": "S13",
      "start": 58.555,
      "speech_end": 60.665,
      "end": 63.065,
      "dur": 4.51,
      "text": "Carrying a lot, a long way, doesn't."
    },
    {
      "id": "S14",
      "start": 63.065,
      "speech_end": 65.091,
      "end": 65.891,
      "dur": 2.827,
      "text": "But that's only half the answer."
    },
    {
      "id": "S15",
      "start": 65.891,
      "speech_end": 69.753,
      "end": 70.353,
      "dur": 4.461,
      "text": "A job that never goes away is no use if the plane wears out."
    },
    {
      "id": "S16",
      "start": 70.353,
      "speech_end": 73.83,
      "end": 74.63,
      "dur": 4.277,
      "text": "And the B-52 has had three completely different jobs."
    },
    {
      "id": "S17",
      "start": 74.63,
      "speech_end": 79.63,
      "end": 82.23,
      "dur": 7.6,
      "text": "To see how it survived all three, we need to go back to a hotel room in Ohio."
    },
    {
      "id": "S18",
      "start": 82.23,
      "speech_end": 85.837,
      "end": 86.637,
      "dur": 4.407,
      "text": "October 1948. Dayton, Ohio."
    },
    {
      "id": "S19",
      "start": 86.637,
      "speech_end": 91.309,
      "end": 92.109,
      "dur": 5.472,
      "text": "A team of Boeing engineers had come to show the Air Force their design for a new bomber."
    },
    {
      "id": "S20",
      "start": 92.109,
      "speech_end": 96.485,
      "end": 97.285,
      "dur": 5.175,
      "text": "It had propellers. And the Air Force wanted to talk about jets."
    },
    {
      "id": "S21",
      "start": 97.285,
      "speech_end": 102.021,
      "end": 102.821,
      "dur": 5.536,
      "text": "So over one weekend, in the Hotel Van Cleve, the engineers redesigned it."
    },
    {
      "id": "S22",
      "start": 102.821,
      "speech_end": 105.082,
      "end": 105.882,
      "dur": 3.061,
      "text": "Swept wings. Eight jet engines."
    },
    {
      "id": "S23",
      "start": 105.882,
      "speech_end": 109.893,
      "end": 110.693,
      "dur": 4.811,
      "text": "One of them went to a hobby shop, bought some balsa wood, and carved a model."
    },
    {
      "id": "S24",
      "start": 110.693,
      "speech_end": 114.106,
      "end": 114.406,
      "dur": 3.713,
      "text": "On Monday, they handed over a thirty-three-page proposal"
    },
    {
      "id": "S25",
      "start": 114.406,
      "speech_end": 116.731,
      "end": 117.531,
      "dur": 3.125,
      "text": "and a model you could hold in one hand."
    },
    {
      "id": "S26",
      "start": 117.531,
      "speech_end": 119.75,
      "end": 120.55,
      "dur": 3.019,
      "text": "That model became the B-52."
    },
    {
      "id": "S27",
      "start": 120.55,
      "speech_end": 127.4,
      "end": 130.0,
      "dur": 9.45,
      "text": "It first flew in 1952. By 1962, Boeing had built seven hundred and forty-four of them."
    },
    {
      "id": "S28",
      "start": 130.0,
      "speech_end": 132.411,
      "end": 133.211,
      "dur": 3.211,
      "text": "Its first job was simple, and terrible."
    },
    {
      "id": "S29",
      "start": 133.211,
      "speech_end": 137.947,
      "end": 138.747,
      "dur": 5.536,
      "text": "Fly very high, very far, into the Soviet Union, and drop nuclear bombs."
    },
    {
      "id": "S30",
      "start": 138.747,
      "speech_end": 140.816,
      "end": 141.616,
      "dur": 2.869,
      "text": "Altitude was its protection."
    },
    {
      "id": "S31",
      "start": 141.616,
      "speech_end": 146.928,
      "end": 147.228,
      "dur": 5.612,
      "text": "Then, in 1960, a Soviet missile shot down an American U-2 spy plane,"
    },
    {
      "id": "S32",
      "start": 147.228,
      "speech_end": 149.916,
      "end": 150.716,
      "dur": 3.488,
      "text": "flying far higher than the B-52 could."
    },
    {
      "id": "S33",
      "start": 150.716,
      "speech_end": 153.146,
      "end": 155.346,
      "dur": 4.63,
      "text": "Flying high had stopped being safe."
    },
    {
      "id": "S34",
      "start": 155.346,
      "speech_end": 161.385,
      "end": 162.185,
      "dur": 6.839,
      "text": "And that giant, three times the speed of sound, was already on the drawing board. The Valkyrie."
    },
    {
      "id": "S35",
      "start": 162.185,
      "speech_end": 168.372,
      "end": 169.172,
      "dur": 6.987,
      "text": "It was designed to cross into Soviet airspace more than twenty kilometres up, faster than a rifle bullet."
    },
    {
      "id": "S36",
      "start": 169.172,
      "speech_end": 174.952,
      "end": 177.352,
      "dur": 8.18,
      "text": "The perfect answer to a question that had just stopped mattering. Only two were ever built."
    },
    {
      "id": "S37",
      "start": 177.352,
      "speech_end": 181.087,
      "end": 181.887,
      "dur": 4.535,
      "text": "The B-52 did something else. It went low."
    },
    {
      "id": "S38",
      "start": 181.887,
      "speech_end": 186.815,
      "end": 187.615,
      "dur": 5.728,
      "text": "Crews trained to fly it a few hundred feet above the ground, under the enemy's radar."
    },
    {
      "id": "S39",
      "start": 187.615,
      "speech_end": 189.023,
      "end": 189.823,
      "dur": 2.208,
      "text": "Job number two."
    },
    {
      "id": "S40",
      "start": 189.823,
      "speech_end": 195.948,
      "end": 196.748,
      "dur": 6.925,
      "text": "It wasn't designed for that. The air near the ground is rough, and a big wing gets shaken for hours."
    },
    {
      "id": "S41",
      "start": 196.748,
      "speech_end": 206.268,
      "end": 208.468,
      "dur": 11.72,
      "text": "On one test flight in 1964, over the Rocky Mountains, turbulence tore most of the tail fin off a B-52. The crew still landed it."
    },
    {
      "id": "S42",
      "start": 208.468,
      "speech_end": 212.671,
      "end": 213.271,
      "dur": 4.803,
      "text": "And by the 1970s, even flying low was getting dangerous."
    },
    {
      "id": "S43",
      "start": 213.271,
      "speech_end": 221.185,
      "end": 221.985,
      "dur": 8.715,
      "text": "So in 1977, the United States cancelled the first version of the B-1, the plane meant to replace the B-52."
    },
    {
      "id": "S44",
      "start": 221.985,
      "speech_end": 225.763,
      "end": 226.563,
      "dur": 4.578,
      "text": "One big reason was a new weapon. The cruise missile."
    },
    {
      "id": "S45",
      "start": 226.563,
      "speech_end": 231.534,
      "end": 232.034,
      "dur": 5.471,
      "text": "A cruise missile flies itself, low and alone, for more than two thousand kilometres."
    },
    {
      "id": "S46",
      "start": 232.034,
      "speech_end": 235.277,
      "end": 236.077,
      "dur": 4.043,
      "text": "So the bomber no longer had to get anywhere near its target."
    },
    {
      "id": "S47",
      "start": 236.077,
      "speech_end": 239.981,
      "end": 240.781,
      "dur": 4.704,
      "text": "It just had to carry the missiles to the edge of the map, and let go."
    },
    {
      "id": "S48",
      "start": 240.781,
      "speech_end": 242.21,
      "end": 242.81,
      "dur": 2.029,
      "text": "Job number three."
    },
    {
      "id": "S49",
      "start": 242.81,
      "speech_end": 246.031,
      "end": 246.831,
      "dur": 4.021,
      "text": "And for this job, the B-52 was almost perfect."
    },
    {
      "id": "S50",
      "start": 246.831,
      "speech_end": 249.391,
      "end": 250.191,
      "dur": 3.36,
      "text": "It can carry up to twenty of those missiles."
    },
    {
      "id": "S51",
      "start": 250.191,
      "speech_end": 254.268,
      "end": 255.068,
      "dur": 4.877,
      "text": "It didn't need to be fast. It didn't need to be invisible."
    },
    {
      "id": "S52",
      "start": 255.068,
      "speech_end": 257.777,
      "end": 258.177,
      "dur": 3.109,
      "text": "It needed to be big, and to fly a long way."
    },
    {
      "id": "S53",
      "start": 258.177,
      "speech_end": 262.785,
      "end": 263.585,
      "dur": 5.408,
      "text": "Which is exactly what those engineers in Dayton had drawn in 1948."
    },
    {
      "id": "S54",
      "start": 263.585,
      "speech_end": 265.676,
      "end": 266.276,
      "dur": 2.691,
      "text": "Three completely different jobs."
    },
    {
      "id": "S55",
      "start": 266.276,
      "speech_end": 269.206,
      "end": 272.006,
      "dur": 5.73,
      "text": "And all three needed the same thing from the plane."
    },
    {
      "id": "S56",
      "start": 272.006,
      "speech_end": 274.694,
      "end": 275.294,
      "dur": 3.288,
      "text": "But even the perfect truck wears out eventually."
    },
    {
      "id": "S57",
      "start": 275.294,
      "speech_end": 279.283,
      "end": 280.283,
      "dur": 4.989,
      "text": "So how is a plane built in the early 1960s still flying at all?"
    },
    {
      "id": "S58",
      "start": 280.283,
      "speech_end": 283.995,
      "end": 284.795,
      "dur": 4.512,
      "text": "Because a wing wears out mostly by flying, not by the calendar."
    },
    {
      "id": "S59",
      "start": 284.795,
      "speech_end": 290.28,
      "end": 291.08,
      "dur": 6.285,
      "text": "Every take-off, every gust, every landing flexes it. And the metal keeps count."
    },
    {
      "id": "S60",
      "start": 291.08,
      "speech_end": 295.048,
      "end": 295.848,
      "dur": 4.768,
      "text": "A busy airliner can fly three or four thousand hours in a single year."
    },
    {
      "id": "S61",
      "start": 295.848,
      "speech_end": 298.301,
      "end": 299.101,
      "dur": 3.253,
      "text": "A B-52 flies a few hundred."
    },
    {
      "id": "S62",
      "start": 299.101,
      "speech_end": 302.749,
      "end": 303.549,
      "dur": 4.448,
      "text": "For most of the Cold War, part of the fleet wasn't flying at all."
    },
    {
      "id": "S63",
      "start": 303.549,
      "speech_end": 306.856,
      "end": 307.156,
      "dur": 3.607,
      "text": "It sat on alert, at the end of the runway, fuelled and armed,"
    },
    {
      "id": "S64",
      "start": 307.156,
      "speech_end": 310.612,
      "end": 311.412,
      "dur": 4.256,
      "text": "with crews sleeping nearby, ready to take off within minutes."
    },
    {
      "id": "S65",
      "start": 311.412,
      "speech_end": 314.484,
      "end": 316.884,
      "dur": 5.472,
      "text": "Waiting barely wears out a wing. Flying does."
    },
    {
      "id": "S66",
      "start": 316.884,
      "speech_end": 322.068,
      "end": 322.868,
      "dur": 5.984,
      "text": "By 2016, the average B-52 had flown about eighteen thousand hours."
    },
    {
      "id": "S67",
      "start": 322.868,
      "speech_end": 326.473,
      "end": 327.073,
      "dur": 4.205,
      "text": "Its wings were estimated to last at least thirty-two thousand."
    },
    {
      "id": "S68",
      "start": 327.073,
      "speech_end": 332.773,
      "end": 335.373,
      "dur": 8.3,
      "text": "So by the measure that matters, the average B-52 had used up only about half its wing."
    },
    {
      "id": "S69",
      "start": 335.373,
      "speech_end": 339.939,
      "end": 340.439,
      "dur": 5.065,
      "text": "And when a fire wrecked one in 2014, the Air Force didn't order a new one."
    },
    {
      "id": "S70",
      "start": 340.439,
      "speech_end": 342.935,
      "end": 343.235,
      "dur": 2.796,
      "text": "Instead, it went to the Arizona desert,"
    },
    {
      "id": "S71",
      "start": 343.235,
      "speech_end": 346.883,
      "end": 347.183,
      "dur": 3.948,
      "text": "picked a B-52 that had been sitting in the sun for seven years,"
    },
    {
      "id": "S72",
      "start": 347.183,
      "speech_end": 351.793,
      "end": 352.593,
      "dur": 5.41,
      "text": "rebuilt it, and sent it back to work. Its nickname is Ghost Rider."
    },
    {
      "id": "S73",
      "start": 352.593,
      "speech_end": 355.067,
      "end": 355.867,
      "dur": 3.275,
      "text": "A few years later, a second one followed."
    },
    {
      "id": "S74",
      "start": 355.867,
      "speech_end": 360.307,
      "end": 361.107,
      "dur": 5.239,
      "text": "It helps that so many were built. Seven hundred and forty-four."
    },
    {
      "id": "S75",
      "start": 361.107,
      "speech_end": 363.752,
      "end": 365.952,
      "dur": 4.845,
      "text": "Of the B-2, there were only ever twenty-one."
    },
    {
      "id": "S76",
      "start": 365.952,
      "speech_end": 369.664,
      "end": 370.464,
      "dur": 4.512,
      "text": "And the B-52 is the cheapest bomber for the Air Force to fly."
    },
    {
      "id": "S77",
      "start": 370.464,
      "speech_end": 374.88,
      "end": 375.68,
      "dur": 5.216,
      "text": "An hour in a B-52 costs less than an hour in a B-1 or a B-2."
    },
    {
      "id": "S78",
      "start": 375.68,
      "speech_end": 383.62,
      "end": 386.22,
      "dur": 10.54,
      "text": "When the job is carrying missiles to the edge of the map, what matters isn't being hard to see. It's how much you carry, and how far."
    },
    {
      "id": "S79",
      "start": 386.22,
      "speech_end": 388.08,
      "end": 388.88,
      "dur": 2.66,
      "text": "But here's the strange part."
    },
    {
      "id": "S80",
      "start": 388.88,
      "speech_end": 393.637,
      "end": 394.437,
      "dur": 5.557,
      "text": "A lot of what's inside a B-52 today didn't exist in 1962."
    },
    {
      "id": "S81",
      "start": 394.437,
      "speech_end": 398.277,
      "end": 399.077,
      "dur": 4.64,
      "text": "Radios, navigation, computers, cockpit screens, weapons."
    },
    {
      "id": "S82",
      "start": 399.077,
      "speech_end": 401.445,
      "end": 402.245,
      "dur": 3.168,
      "text": "All replaced, some of them more than once."
    },
    {
      "id": "S83",
      "start": 402.245,
      "speech_end": 406.917,
      "end": 407.517,
      "dur": 5.272,
      "text": "A new radar is being fitted, based on the radar of a modern fighter jet."
    },
    {
      "id": "S84",
      "start": 407.517,
      "speech_end": 409.177,
      "end": 409.977,
      "dur": 2.46,
      "text": "And next come the engines."
    },
    {
      "id": "S85",
      "start": 409.977,
      "speech_end": 413.604,
      "end": 414.404,
      "dur": 4.427,
      "text": "The ones it flies on now were designed in the 1950s."
    },
    {
      "id": "S86",
      "start": 414.404,
      "speech_end": 418.073,
      "end": 418.373,
      "dur": 3.969,
      "text": "They're being replaced by Rolls-Royce engines from the same family"
    },
    {
      "id": "S87",
      "start": 418.373,
      "speech_end": 420.677,
      "end": 421.477,
      "dur": 3.104,
      "text": "that powers Gulfstream business jets."
    },
    {
      "id": "S88",
      "start": 421.477,
      "speech_end": 424.615,
      "end": 425.415,
      "dur": 3.937,
      "text": "Eight old engines out. Eight new ones in."
    },
    {
      "id": "S89",
      "start": 425.415,
      "speech_end": 428.103,
      "end": 428.903,
      "dur": 3.488,
      "text": "Why not four bigger ones, like a modern airliner?"
    },
    {
      "id": "S90",
      "start": 428.903,
      "speech_end": 431.953,
      "end": 432.753,
      "dur": 3.851,
      "text": "Because that would turn an engine swap into a redesign."
    },
    {
      "id": "S91",
      "start": 432.753,
      "speech_end": 443.081,
      "end": 443.381,
      "dur": 10.627,
      "text": "Losing one big engine on take-off would pull the plane hard to one side, so it would need a new rudder. It would also need new cockpit controls, changes to the wing,"
    },
    {
      "id": "S92",
      "start": 443.381,
      "speech_end": 445.401,
      "end": 446.201,
      "dur": 2.82,
      "text": "and years of new flight tests."
    },
    {
      "id": "S93",
      "start": 446.201,
      "speech_end": 449.031,
      "end": 451.431,
      "dur": 5.23,
      "text": "Eight smaller engines avoid most of that."
    },
    {
      "id": "S94",
      "start": 451.431,
      "speech_end": 455.763,
      "end": 456.563,
      "dur": 5.133,
      "text": "The upgraded plane gets a new letter. The B-52J."
    },
    {
      "id": "S95",
      "start": 456.563,
      "speech_end": 459.742,
      "end": 462.342,
      "dur": 5.779,
      "text": "Its test flights are planned for the end of the 2020s."
    },
    {
      "id": "S96",
      "start": 462.342,
      "speech_end": 467.441,
      "end": 468.041,
      "dur": 5.699,
      "text": "Meanwhile, the Air Force is buying a brand-new stealth bomber, the B-21 Raider."
    },
    {
      "id": "S97",
      "start": 468.041,
      "speech_end": 471.262,
      "end": 472.062,
      "dur": 4.021,
      "text": "And the long-term plan is a bomber fleet of just two types."
    },
    {
      "id": "S98",
      "start": 472.062,
      "speech_end": 474.067,
      "end": 474.867,
      "dur": 2.805,
      "text": "Not the B-1. Not the B-2."
    },
    {
      "id": "S99",
      "start": 474.867,
      "speech_end": 476.958,
      "end": 477.758,
      "dur": 2.891,
      "text": "The newest bomber, and the oldest."
    },
    {
      "id": "S100",
      "start": 477.758,
      "speech_end": 479.529,
      "end": 480.329,
      "dur": 2.571,
      "text": "One gets in, unseen."
    },
    {
      "id": "S101",
      "start": 480.329,
      "speech_end": 482.919,
      "end": 485.719,
      "dur": 5.39,
      "text": "The other carries a lot, from far away."
    },
    {
      "id": "S102",
      "start": 485.719,
      "speech_end": 488.364,
      "end": 489.764,
      "dur": 4.045,
      "text": "So why is the B-52 still flying?"
    },
    {
      "id": "S103",
      "start": 489.764,
      "speech_end": 492.473,
      "end": 493.273,
      "dur": 3.509,
      "text": "Not because it was the best bomber ever built."
    },
    {
      "id": "S104",
      "start": 493.273,
      "speech_end": 496.836,
      "end": 497.636,
      "dur": 4.363,
      "text": "It was never the fastest, the highest, or the hardest to see."
    },
    {
      "id": "S105",
      "start": 497.636,
      "speech_end": 500.388,
      "end": 501.188,
      "dur": 3.552,
      "text": "Its replacements were built around a technology."
    },
    {
      "id": "S106",
      "start": 501.188,
      "speech_end": 503.748,
      "end": 504.548,
      "dur": 3.36,
      "text": "The B-52 was built around a job."
    },
    {
      "id": "S107",
      "start": 504.548,
      "speech_end": 508.326,
      "end": 511.326,
      "dur": 6.778,
      "text": "The technology kept expiring. The job never did."
    },
    {
      "id": "S108",
      "start": 511.326,
      "speech_end": 515.891,
      "end": 516.191,
      "dur": 4.865,
      "text": "And everything that did go out of date, the engines, the electronics, the weapons,"
    },
    {
      "id": "S109",
      "start": 516.191,
      "speech_end": 518.453,
      "end": 519.253,
      "dur": 3.061,
      "text": "turned out to be the parts you could swap."
    },
    {
      "id": "S110",
      "start": 519.253,
      "speech_end": 524.074,
      "end": 524.874,
      "dur": 5.621,
      "text": "What's left of the 1948 design is the part that's hardest to replace."
    },
    {
      "id": "S111",
      "start": 524.874,
      "speech_end": 528.034,
      "end": 530.834,
      "dur": 5.96,
      "text": "A big, strong wing that carries a lot, a long way."
    },
    {
      "id": "S112",
      "start": 530.834,
      "speech_end": 532.669,
      "end": 533.669,
      "dur": 2.835,
      "text": "So here's a question for you."
    },
    {
      "id": "S113",
      "start": 533.669,
      "speech_end": 536.463,
      "end": 537.063,
      "dur": 3.395,
      "text": "What do you think will finally ground the B-52?"
    },
    {
      "id": "S114",
      "start": 537.063,
      "speech_end": 541.303,
      "end": 543.303,
      "dur": 6.24,
      "text": "A better plane, or a job it can't do? Let me know in the comments."
    }
  ]
}